ṇ. 78","q":"Cāṇ"},{"t":"txt","s":";\n so त्रिगुण; शतगुणीभवति becomes a hundred-fold, अध्यर्धगुणमाहुर्यं\n बले शौर्ये च केशव "},{"t":"cite","s":"Mb. 11. 20. 1","q":"Mb"},{"t":"txt","s":"."}]},{"n":"15","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"A secondary element, a subordinate part (opp. मुख्य); न च\n गुणानुग्रहार्थं प्रधानस्यावृत्तिर्युक्ता ŚB. on "},{"t":"cite","s":"MS. 12. 1. 4","q":"MS"},{"t":"txt","s":"."}]},{"n":"16","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Excess, abundance, superfluity; पराङ्मुखवधं कृत्वा कोऽत्र प्राप्तस्त्वया\n गुणः "},{"t":"cite","s":"Rām. 4. 17. 16","q":"Rām"},{"t":"txt","s":"."}]},{"n":"17","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"An adjective, a word subordinate to another in a sentence."}]},{"n":"18","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"The substitution of ए, ओ, अर् and अल् for इ, उ, ऋ (short\n or long) and ऌ, or the vowels अ, ए, ओ and अर् and अल्."}]},{"n":"19","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"(In Rhet.) Quality considered as an inherent property of a Rasa\n or sentiment. Mammaṭa thus defines गुण:− ये रहस्याङ्गिनो धर्माः\n शौर्यादय इवात्मनः । उत्कर्षहेतवस्ते स्युरचलस्थितयो गुणाः ॥ K. "},{"t":"cite","s":"P. 8","q":"P"},{"t":"txt","s":".\n (Some writers on rhetoric, such as Vāmana, Jagannātha Paṇḍita,\n Daṇḍin and others, consider Guṇas to be properties both of शब्द\n and अर्थ, and mention ten varieties under each head. Mammaṭa, however,\n recognises only three, and, after discussing and criticizing the views\n of others, says: माधुर्यैजःप्रसादाख्यास्त्रयस्ते न पुनर्दश K. "},{"t":"cite","s":"P. 8","q":"P"},{"t":"txt","s":"); "},{"t":"cite","s":"Ki. 17. 6","q":"Ki"},{"t":"txt","s":".\n[]"}]},{"n":"20","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"(In gram. and Mīm.) Property considered as the meaning of a class\n of words; e. g. grammarians recognise four kinds of the meaning of\n words; जाति, गुण, क्रिया and द्रव्य, and give गौः, शुक्लः, चलः\n and डित्थः as instances to illustrate these meanings."}]},{"n":"21","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"(In politics) A proper course of action, an expedient. (The expedients\n to be used by a king in foreign politics are six:− 1 सन्धि peace\n or alliance; 2 विग्रह war; 3 यान march or expedition; 4 स्थान\n or आसन halt; 5 संश्रय seeking shelter; 6 द्वैध or द्वैधीभाव\n duplicity; सन्धिर्ना विग्रहो यानमासनं द्वैधमाश्रयः Ak.) see "},{"t":"cite","s":"Y. 1. 346","q":"Y"},{"t":"txt","s":"; "},{"t":"cite","s":"Ms. 7. 160","q":"Ms"},{"t":"txt","s":";\n Śi. 2. 26; "},{"t":"cite","s":"R. 8. 21","q":"R"},{"t":"txt","s":"."}]},{"n":"22","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"The number ‘three’ (derived from the three qualities)."}]},{"n":"23","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"The chord of an arc (in geom.)."}]},{"n":"24","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"An organ of sense."}]},{"n":"25","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"A subordinate dish; "},{"t":"cite","s":"Ms. 3. 226, 233","q":"Ms"},{"t":"txt","s":"."}]},{"n":"26","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"A cook."}]},{"n":"27","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"An epithet of Bhīma as in युधिष्ठिरोऽपि गुणप्रियः Vās."}]},{"n":"28","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Leaving, abandonment."}]},{"n":"29","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"A multiplier, coefficient (in math.)"}]},{"n":"30","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Division, subdivision, species, kind."}]},{"n":"31","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"The peculiar property of letters which are pronounced with external\n utterance (बाह्यप्रयत्न); they are eleven.\n.━{@Comp.@}: गुणाग्र्यम्, गुणागुणः, गुणातीत, गुणाधिष्ठानकम्, गुणानुबन्धित्वम्, गुणानुरागः, गुणानुरोधः, गुणान्तरम्, गुणान्वित, गुणोपपन्न, गुणयुक्त, गुणसंपन्न, गुणापवादः, गुणनिन्दा, गुणाभिधानम्, गुणाकरः, गुणाढ्य, गुणात्मन्, गुणाधारः, गुणाश्रय, गुणेश्वरः, गुणोत्कर्षः, गुणोत्कीर्तनम्, गुणोत्कृष्ट, गुणोपेत, गुणौघः, गुणौघम्, गुणकथनम्, गुणकर्तृत्वम्, गुणकर्मन्, गुणकर्मविभाग, गुणकल्पना, गुणकाण्डः, गुणकार, गुणकीर्तनम्, गुणश्लाघा, गुणस्तुतिः, गुणकृत्यम्, गुणगणः, गुणगानम्, गुणगृध्नु, गुणगृह्य, गुणगौरी, गुणग्रहणम्, गुणग्रहीतृ, गुणग्राहक, गुणग्राहिन्, गुणग्रामः, गुणघातिन्, गुणज्ञ, गुणत्रयम्, गुणत्रितयम्, गुणदोषौ, गुणधर्मः, गुणनिधिः, गुणपदी, गुणपूगम्, गुणप्रकर्षः, गुणभावः, गुणभोक्तृ, गुणमहत्, गुणमुष्टिः, गुणरागः, गुणराशिः, गुण